{align:center|# LITURGY OF REPENTANCE & RECITATION OF THE AVATAṂSAKA SŪTRA}
{align:center|*(Pre-Chanting Repentance and Recitation Ritual)*}

{align:center|*(Chanting the sacred scriptures with pure body, speech, and mind yields measureless blessings and virtue; therefore, one should sincerely repent before recitation to completely purify the three karmas.)*}

{align:center|Namo all Buddhas throughout the ten directions and the entirety of empty space. (1 bow)}
{align:center|Namo the Honored Dharma throughout the ten directions and the entirety of empty space. (1 bow)}
{align:center|Namo all Sangha of Noble Worthies and Sages throughout the ten directions and the entirety of empty space. (1 bow)}

{align:center|*(Kneel, holding incense to make offerings and aspirations)*:}

{align:center|May this cloud of wondrous fragrant incense
Pervade the realms of the ten directions,
Offered up to all the Buddhas,
The Honored Dharma, and all Bodhisattvas,
Limitless Śrāvakas and Pratyekabuddhas,
And all Noble Sages and Superior Worthies.
Manifesting as a luminous dais of light,
Encompassing limitless, boundless worlds,
Perfuming all living beings,
Inspiring each to bring forth the supreme Bodhi Mind,
Leaving behind all unwholesome karmic delusions,
And together perfecting the Unexcelled Way.}

{align:center|**NAMO INCENSE OFFERING BODHISATTVA MAHASATTVA.** (3 times)}

{align:center|*(Bow 1 time, kneel, join palms, and sincerely prostrate)*:}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Dharma Realm of True Suchness,
Vairocana Tathāgata,
The Pure Dharmakāya,
And all Buddhas throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Lotus Store World of Perfect Fruition,
Vairocana Tathāgata,
The Complete and Perfect Saṃbhogakāya,
And all Buddhas throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Transformation Realms of the Ten Directions,
Śākyamuni Tathāgata,
The Infinite Nirmāṇakāya,
And all Buddhas throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Western Land of Ultimate Bliss,
Amitābha Tathāgata,
Whose sea-like marks and subtle dust-mote virtues adorn the worlds,
And all Buddhas throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Western Land of Peace and Bliss,
Amitābha Tathāgata,
Whose transformation bodies reach the ten directions,
And all Buddhas throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Western Land of Peace and Bliss,
The profound teachings and principles of the Mahāyāna Sūtras,
Revealing the fullness of primary and secondary rewards,
And the Honored Dharma throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Western Land of Peace and Bliss,
Bodhisattva Avalokiteśvara,
Of purple-golden form and myriad billion transformations,
And all Bodhisattvas throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Western Land of Peace and Bliss,
Bodhisattva Mahāsthāmaprāpta,
Whose radiant wisdom shines boundlessly,
And all Bodhisattvas throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|With Utmost Sincerity, We Prostrate:
To the Western Land of Peace and Bliss,
The Pure Ocean-Wide Assembly,
Adorned with the twofold perfection of blessings and wisdom,
And all the Noble Assembly throughout the Dharma Realm. (1 bow)}

{align:center|*(Stand, palms joined, and make this resolve)*:
I now, on behalf of the four debts of kindness, beings of the three realms, and all living beings across the Dharma Realm, vow to eradicate the three obstacles, take refuge, and sincerely repent. (1 bow)}

{align:center|**SINCERE REPENTANCE**}

{align:justify|I, disciple [Name / Dharma Name], together with all living beings across the Dharma Realm, from beginningless time until today, shrouded in ignorance, have been deluded and confused. Driven by the six sense organs and the three karmas, habituated to unwholesome deeds, we have broadly transgressed the ten evil actions, the five unpardonable offenses, and countless other sins, boundless and beyond reckoning.}

{align:justify|The Buddhas of the ten directions ever abide in the world, the sounds of Dharma never cease, celestial fragrances fill the air, the flavor of Truth abounds, and pure radiant light illuminates all without barrier. The wondrous, eternal Truth fills the vast expanse of space.}

{align:justify|Yet from beginningless time, my six senses have been blind and my three karmas darkened; neither seeing, nor hearing, nor knowing, I have drifted ceaselessly through the cycle of birth and death, passing through painful evil paths for hundreds of thousands of myriad kalpas without release. As the Sūtra says: 'The body of Vairocana Buddha pervades all places; the dwelling of the Buddha is called Eternally Quiescent Light; thus know that all dharmas are the Buddha Dharma.' Yet blind to this, I followed the stream of ignorance, perceiving impurity within Bodhi wisdom and generating bondage within liberation.}

{align:justify|Now I awaken, now I renounce and repent. Reverently before all Buddhas and Amitābha the World-Honored One, I openly disclose and repent: May all heavy offenses created through the three karmas and six senses from beginningless time, in the present, or in the future—whether committed by myself, or causing others to commit them, or rejoicing in others' wrongdoing; whether remembered or forgotten, known or unknown, doubted or undoubting, concealed or unconcealed—be thoroughly purified and dissolved without residue.}

{align:justify|Having repented, may my six sense organs and three karmas be stainless and faultless, and all wholesome roots cultivated be utterly pure. Universally dedicating this merit to adorn the Pure Land, may I and all living beings be reborn together in the Land of Peaceful Sustenance.}

{align:justify|May Amitābha Buddha ever protect and guide me, causing my wholesome roots to grow vigorously in this present life, never losing affinities with the Pure Land. At the moment of death, may my body be peaceful and my right mindfulness steadfast; with sight and hearing clear, may I behold Amitābha Buddha and the Holy Assembly holding a flower dais to welcome me, in a single instant reborn before the Buddha, perfected in the Bodhisattva Way, broadly delivering all sentient beings that all may together achieve Buddhahood.}

{align:center|Having repented and made vows, we take refuge and bow:
**Namo Western Land of Ultimate Bliss, Great Kindness and Great Compassion Amitābha Tathāgata, and the Triple Gem throughout the Dharma Realm.** (1 bow)}

{align:center|**INCENSE PRAISE**}

{align:center|Sandalwood ignites within the censer,
Fragrant smoke billows to myriad distant realms.
With profound and earnest reverence,
We pray the Buddhas compassionately witness our sincere devotion.}

{align:center|**NAMO INCENSE CLOUD CANOPY BODHISATTVA MAHASATTVA.** (3 times)}

{align:center|**MANTRA FOR PURIFYING THE DHARMA REALM**}
{align:center|Oṃ raṃ svāhā. (Recite 7 times)}

{align:center|**MANTRA FOR PURIFYING SPEECH KARMA**}
{align:center|Oṃ śucite śucite mahā-śucite śuśucite svāhā. (Recite 3 times)}

{align:center|**MANTRA FOR PURIFYING THE THREE KARMAS**}
{align:center|Oṃ svabhāva-śuddhāḥ sarva-dharmāḥ svabhāva-śuddho 'ham. (Recite 3 times)}

{align:center|**UNIVERSAL OFFERING MANTRA**}
{align:center|Oṃ gagana-saṃbhava vajra hoḥ. (Recite 3 times)}

{align:center|**ASPIRATION VERSE FOR CHANTING THE AVATAṂSAKA SŪTRA**}

{align:center|Namo Ever-Abiding Triple Gem of the Ten Directions. (3 times)}

{align:center|Bowing to the Honored One of the Three Realms,
Taking refuge with the Buddhas of the ten directions.
I now bring forth this vast resolve:
To uphold and recite the Avataṃsaka Sūtra.
Above, to repay the Four Great Kindnesses,
Below, to relieve the suffering of the Three Destinies.
May all who see or hear of this
Bring forth the supreme Bodhi Mind,
When this retribution body is fulfilled,
Be reborn together in the Land of Ultimate Bliss.}

{align:center|**NAMO FUNDAMENTAL TEACHER SHAKYAMUNI BUDDHA.** (3 times)}

{align:center|**OPENING GĀTHĀ**}

{align:center|The Supreme, profound, and wondrous Dharma,
In hundreds of thousands of myriad kalpas is rarely encountered.
I now have seen and heard, and am able to receive and uphold it,
May I understand the Tathāgata’s true meaning.}

{align:center|**NAMO AVATAṂSAKA ASSEMBLY BUDDHAS AND BODHISATTVAS MAHASATTVAS.** (3 times)}
